// One workspace, three modules.
//
// The module paths stay github.com/luhtaf/{corator,surisink,s3nitor} rather
// than being rewritten under k8rensic. Rewriting them would break every
// existing import, every published release, and the upstream repositories these
// were merged from — and buys nothing: a workspace already lets the three build
// and test as one tree.
//
// Each keeps its own go.mod because they keep their own dependencies. corator
// pulls in Coraza, s3nitor is pinned to cgo by the SQLite driver, and surisink
// needs neither. Folding them into one module would give every component the
// worst constraint of all three.
go 1.25.0

use (
	./components/corator
	./components/s3nitor
	./components/surisink
)
